WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.860
- But we love people here coming

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.120
to the show with a passion for writing.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.680
I love writing as well.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.050
And you started really young, right?

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.129
- I started writing--
- I mean, you're only, like,

00:00:08.129 --> 00:00:10.350
you're young now but I mean younger, yeah.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.810
- I started writing when I was 12,

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:12.900
so I started writing books.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.820
I always loved to read like many kids.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.380
And 12 was the age where I was like,

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.820
I think I can do this.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:18.960
And the magical part

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.600
about being 12 is I truly
believed I was gonna write a book

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.250
and get published like the next day

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.096
and like be on a show like
this, like the next day.

00:00:25.096 --> 00:00:25.950
But, that's a great thing actually

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:26.783
about being young.

00:00:26.783 --> 00:00:29.400
- It is. It's the best thing
because you only do things

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.080
because you love it when you're that age.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.130
And so I loved to write,

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.900
so I was like I'm gonna write
a book and get published.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.160
And so I wrote the book.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.660
I googled how to get published.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.730
I knew you had to get a literary agent.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:39.930
And I started reaching out

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.270
to agents when I was 12,
like from my bedroom.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.154
And yeah.
(audience cheering)

00:00:44.154 --> 00:00:45.735
- What in the world? That's so cool.

00:00:45.735 --> 00:00:47.820
- Not successfully.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.440
I got hundreds of rejections like

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.273
and it was just the start

00:00:50.273 --> 00:00:51.960
of like the hundreds and
hundreds of rejections.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.480
And my parents had no idea
I was like emailing agents

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.313
in my bedroom.

00:00:55.313 --> 00:00:57.411
Like they had, they were
like, why are you crying?

00:00:57.411 --> 00:00:58.970
I was like no, no reason.

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:01.140
But so, but I knew it was possible.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.610
Like there was a path.
- [Kelly] That's so bold.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.410
- Yeah. So I knew that there was a path

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.150
so I just kept doing it
and writing another book

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.200
and then all the rejections.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.640
And then another one and another one.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:09.960
And by the time I reached college

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.370
I had written like five books.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.240
All of them rejected.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.280
But I felt like I was getting closer

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.750
and there was so much hope.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.030
- Yeah. I love that you,
that says a lot about you.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.410
You see hope outta that situation.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.730
A lot of people would be deterred though.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:21.563
- Yes.
- Like they would.

00:01:21.563 --> 00:01:24.918
But I think some of us, like
I did better as a child too

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:25.860
when I did get a door slammed.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.260
It almost makes you instill
more confidence in yourself

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.160
and your gifts or your talents.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.981
And you go, no, I know this
is what I'm supposed to do.

00:01:30.981 --> 00:01:31.814
- [Alex] Definitely.

00:01:31.814 --> 00:01:33.270
- Some people it drives and I feel like

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.380
that definitely happened.
- It did for me.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.250
- Yeah.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:38.134
I feel like all of us know
rejection well in this industry.

00:01:38.134 --> 00:01:39.085
- [Anna] Yeah.

00:01:39.085 --> 00:01:40.500
- And that sucks.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.570
And it's not always easy to get back up.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.742
- No, it's taken me
down quite a few times.

00:01:44.742 --> 00:01:45.575
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:45.575 --> 00:01:47.236
- Where I've been like, well, it's over.

00:01:47.236 --> 00:01:48.180
- [Anna] Yeah.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.013
Throw in the towel.

00:01:49.013 --> 00:01:50.070
Saw the numbers.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:50.903
It's been fun.

00:01:50.903 --> 00:01:51.960
- [Kelly] Saw the numbers.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.330
- Saw the numbers and it's not great.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.990
- I could only hope that like
my daughters have the drive

00:01:57.990 --> 00:01:59.550
that like what made you,

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.080
where do you think that comes from?

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.780
- I mean, my mom is an
immigrant from Colombia

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.580
and like my dad, like
didn't go to college.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:09.390
Like he, I watched my parents
like, have to work so hard

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.670
and they always told us
like, you can do anything.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:14.520
You just have to keep working
really hard and like--

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.353
- Wow.

00:02:15.353 --> 00:02:16.186
- And they were so supportive.

00:02:16.186 --> 00:02:17.400
Like they paid for our
college and everything.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.990
So like they're so much privilege in that,

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:20.130
like to be able to go to college

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.600
and like have a support system.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.520
And have them like really
believe from the beginning.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.870
Like they did eventually find out

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.361
I was emailing agents after, like,

00:02:26.361 --> 00:02:28.410
after I went to school for it

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.270
and I went to college for writing.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.818
- That's when they found out?

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:34.110
(laughing)

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:36.660
- What is my daughter doing
in her bedroom right now?

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:37.530
Like, I'm like what?

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:38.790
- Yeah, always on the computer.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:41.280
And so they really did
like support my dream

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.140
and believe in me.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.610
But yet it was really tough.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.310
Like I'm sure seeing your kid
go through so many rejections.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.860
Obviously I'm so glad I didn't stop.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.410
But it is tough to see
that and to experience it.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.300
But I always just
believed it would happen.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.460
Just not the way it happened, I guess.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.680
- Yeah. I love the way it happened.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.330
So before you tell us how you were able

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:01.590
to finally get published.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.060
Can you share what the book's about?

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:03.893
- [Alex] Sure.

00:03:03.893 --> 00:03:04.726
- I love this.
- Yes.

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:06.300
So it's called "Lightlark".

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.920
It's a young adult fantasy.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.620
It's about an island that
appears every hundred years

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.570
to host a game where six rulers fight

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:14.010
to break their deadly curses.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.240
So every ruler

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.215
has a different curse.
- I'm in.

00:03:17.215 --> 00:03:18.150
I wanna to see the movie.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:19.195
- Yeah.

00:03:19.195 --> 00:03:20.028
- I want the whole series.
- [Alex.] Yeah.

00:03:20.028 --> 00:03:20.861
- I love stuff like this.

00:03:20.861 --> 00:03:22.380
- All of the curses are uniquely wicked.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.490
And to break all of them,

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:24.960
one of the six rulers has to die

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.370
and one will win a bunch of power.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.295
- Damn. Okay.

00:03:27.295 --> 00:03:28.290
- So there's like betrayals,
there's plot twists.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:29.220
You don't know who's lying,

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.053
who's telling the truth
(gasps)

00:03:30.053 --> 00:03:31.230
until the very last page.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:32.063
- This girl.

00:03:32.063 --> 00:03:32.896
- I know.

00:03:32.896 --> 00:03:33.729
- Are you casting?

00:03:33.729 --> 00:03:35.079
- [Kelly] Finally!

00:03:35.079 --> 00:03:36.023
- Yes and yes.
- [Kelly] I was like,

00:03:36.023 --> 00:03:37.494
I have a couple actors.

00:03:37.494 --> 00:03:39.783
- Yes, absolutely. Yes.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.133
- Oh my god, that's really cool.

00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:43.530
- Thank you. Thank you.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.940
- I can't believe you got turned down.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.440
It's like such a great idea.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.660
And a lot of people love that field.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.320
We love that fiction and it's
nice escapism from reality.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.270
Some of the parallels
can be similar sometimes.

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.250
When publishers rejected "Lightlark,"

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.920
Alex put, she put
together this TikTok video

00:03:58.920 --> 00:03:59.789
and I gotta show you.

00:03:59.789 --> 00:04:02.706
(boisterous music)

00:04:14.421 --> 00:04:15.660
(clapping)

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:19.140
Like, I feel like what that
is is like a vision board

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:21.510
for like what do we want
the film to look like?

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:23.940
Like it was like aesthetically so rad.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:26.790
All the images, my favorite
being that like bridge.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.650
To where? I don't know?

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:29.821
I don't know what that says about me.

00:04:29.821 --> 00:04:31.470
I'll talk about it in therapy later.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.600
But why did you want to post that?

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.260
- So at that point, almost
every publisher had rejected it.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.100
They loved the book,

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.720
but they said this is such a tough market

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.010
and like it's so hard to break through.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:41.843
So they said no.

00:04:41.843 --> 00:04:43.530
And I truly felt like

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.570
if I could just get this out to readers

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:46.403
and ask them like,

00:04:46.403 --> 00:04:47.880
would you read a book about this?

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:48.713
I felt like

00:04:48.713 --> 00:04:50.670
I couldn't be the only one
who would read this book.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:52.050
And I put everything I left into it.

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:54.180
So I posted it, just kind
of like a silent plea

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.013
to the void,

00:04:55.013 --> 00:04:57.060
like, please, please like
someone like see this

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:57.893
and want it.

00:04:57.893 --> 00:05:00.900
And within like five
hours it had no views.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.030
And so I was like, oh my gosh,
I'm proving publishers right.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.368
Like no one wants this book.

00:05:04.368 --> 00:05:05.311
(laughing)

00:05:05.311 --> 00:05:06.630
- And so I almost deleted
it 'cause I was like,

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.560
this is bad.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:08.393
But I left it up.

00:05:08.393 --> 00:05:10.080
I had nothing to lose at that point.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.150
And the next morning
I was in a parking lot

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:15.540
and I randomly checked
the app and it went viral.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.214
It had like over a million views, yeah.

00:05:17.214 --> 00:05:18.276
(applause)

00:05:18.276 --> 00:05:19.109
- [Kelly] So cool.

00:05:19.109 --> 00:05:21.483
- And then a week later
it went to auction.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:26.130
- Yeah, this is me finding
out that it debuted number one

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.480
on the New York Times Best Seller list,

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.743
which is like a dream.

00:05:29.743 --> 00:05:30.576
- [Kelly] It's cool.
- And it's been on there

00:05:30.576 --> 00:05:32.430
for 10 weeks ever since it came out, yeah.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:33.263
- Oh my gosh.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:35.632
- Gives chills.

00:05:35.632 --> 00:05:36.465
- Thank you.

00:05:36.465 --> 00:05:39.900
- Like what a way to take your
power back in the situation.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.300
Because I was telling
her in the commercial,

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.180
like it's a really cool thing

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:46.380
and I can relate in this sense

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:48.780
of like having people
help your career happen.

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:49.650
- [Alex] Yes.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.010
- Like me, like auditioning.

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:51.843
- Yes.

00:05:51.843 --> 00:05:53.850
- And like literally I got
door slammed in my face before.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.500
I had to go on a competition

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.030
to have people like vote for me

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:58.680
and be like, see somebody likes it.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.350
Like, you know, it's like,
and that's the kind of similar

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:03.210
and I love, there's a power to that

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:04.380
and a leverage to that

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:05.460
like in this industry.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:06.758
And I'm so happy for you.

00:06:06.758 --> 00:06:07.723
- Thank you so much.

00:06:07.723 --> 00:06:08.928
(cheering and clapping)

00:06:08.928 --> 00:06:09.761
- [Kelly] Yeah. It's so cool.

00:06:09.761 --> 00:06:10.594
- Thank you.

00:06:10.594 --> 00:06:12.150
- And now you do have a movie deal

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:12.990
as well, right?
- Yes.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:15.030
You know, "Lightlark" is
being made into a movie

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:17.280
by Universal and the
producers of "Twilight,"

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:20.880
which is just, yeah, it's a dream.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.886
- Oh my god.

00:06:21.886 --> 00:06:22.719
- I mean.

00:06:22.719 --> 00:06:23.552
- [ Kelly] I'm like, what's happening?

00:06:23.552 --> 00:06:24.385
- My heart is like

00:06:24.385 --> 00:06:25.218
(mimics explosion).
- It's a dream.

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:26.051
- And just like what you said,

00:06:26.051 --> 00:06:26.970
like I would not be here

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.620
if it wasn't for every single person

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.480
who supported me when no one else did.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:31.590
Like they saw the potential.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:34.350
All of the readers who saw
that video now bought it

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.760
and are hopefully gonna see the movie

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:36.990
and just to have their support.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:37.823
- [Audience] Aw!
- [Alex] Like I'm so,

00:06:37.823 --> 00:06:39.660
I owe it all to them.

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:41.010
- I love it.

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:41.850
It literally is,

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.380
this whole episode is about passion

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.400
like believing in yourself.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.840
That's so cool.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:49.020
I'm, this is such, honestly
this would make a great movie.

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:51.150
Like the whole, like how it started

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:53.550
and how it ended and
like to keep believing

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.020
in yourself when you get knocked down.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:56.250
'Cause we all get doors.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:57.120
Everybody always thinks like,

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.800
oh it was so easy they
did this and it happened.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.797
I'm like, you didn't
see all the pre pre-game

00:07:00.797 --> 00:07:03.300
that happened like, so that's so cool.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.133
I'm so happy for you.

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:04.966
- Thank you so much.

00:07:04.966 --> 00:07:06.060
- I can't wait to hold the series.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:07.140
I wanna read a whole series of it.

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:08.057
I can't wait to see the movie.

00:07:08.057 --> 00:07:09.406
- [Alex] Thank you.
- I'm very excited for you.

00:07:09.406 --> 00:07:10.239
- [Alex] Thank you so much.
- Yeah.

00:07:10.239 --> 00:07:11.560
Thank you for having me.
- And, I know some actors

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.393
(laughing)

00:07:12.393 --> 00:07:13.226
So let's,

00:07:13.226 --> 00:07:14.670
and I'm not one of them,

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:16.320
but I'll write you a pretty song.

